   "date": "2018-12-03",
   "stage_hint": null,
   "brief": "The speaker seconded the Live Sheep Long Haul Export Prohibition Bill 2018 (No. 2), proposing a five-year phase-out of long-haul live sheep exports and a ban on Middle Eastern exports during July–September from 2019, citing community opposition (72.2% support in Wentworth) and the Moss review’s finding that regulation fails community expectations."
